think REDS %747 stood OPEN naming its own door -- a runner that tells could not run from ran and refused -- and it says outright that the runner is the tools/ lane, which is this seat's. Nobody held it on the claim board.
think The claim board also carried my own bakery-suffix-key-assert from last lap, status building, its scan and control parked in stash@{0} rather than in flight. Closed it rather than let a false building line stand six hours.
think Measured the discriminator before claiming rather than reasoning it. In the failing branch of standing_equipment_run.sh a failed capture redirect and a guard that ran and refused both leave the branch at exit 1, run on metal. So the exit status never could tell them apart, and the artifact is what can.
think The evidence write was the whole gap -- tail -n 200 out > evidence.NAME.txt had its exit status discarded, and the echo one line below announced that path either way. That is exactly what the dead pass published: two guards that had run GREEN minutes earlier, each cited to a file the refused write never made.
think /dev/full reproduces the recorded ENOSPC line exactly, so both sides are provable in a pen without filling a shared pier's disk.
think The repair takes the shape gated already took at %374: a fifth verdict, counted apart, refusing the pass and withholding the receipt, since a pass that lost an answer would otherwise publish coverage it never took.
think It spans two files by necessity rather than by scope creep. standing_equipment_scan.sh counted every verdict that was neither green nor gated as red, so a runner emitting a fifth word into a scan that had not been told would re-make the fault one file over. That is the leg blindword_books_a_red.
obs The witness refuses at line 91 on any tree whose card carries a peer's red, and this pier's card carries 19, none mine. Proven PRE-EXISTING rather than assumed -- my four files were set aside, the witness run on unmodified sources, and it refused identically. A probe card of green rows reached my own legs.
obs The ORDER clause cost this lap its cold run, exactly as the clause predicts. Last lap launched a pass near its own close; this lap's round-open pull moved HEAD, and the runner refused a second pass naming the stale launch_head. The pass was stopped through tools/f/fleet_call.sh, which resolved four peer trees and refused every one, reaching this ship's own pid alone.
obs qa_report_card.sh reads a control's CODE as prose. This control's comments alone grade B/82; with its 383 =no leg branches counted as negative sentences it grades C+/78, and it falls further with every honest two-sided leg. Lowering that number means writing one-sided legs, so the reading is named on the card rather than gamed.
